{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"9f96a334a4ce6f6b05b4c9a95746297fd4a222a2dbaa53a29282cabccbdb6599","digest":{"component_or_area":"MCP server initialization","key_entities":["rebar.mcp_server.build_server()","mcp.server.fastmcp.server.Settings","mcp.server.fastmcp.server.FastMCP","Settings.lifespan","Settings.model_rebuild()","pydantic_settings.sources.utils.IncompleteFieldDef","tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_settings_completion.py"],"problem_keywords":["pydantic-settings","forward-reference","unresolved annotation","model rebuild","MCP v1","IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning"],"propositions":["The public build_server() factory emits IncompleteFieldDefinitionWarning on first FastMCP construction when that warning is promoted to error.","MCP v1 defines Settings before FastMCP under postponed annotations, leaving Settings.lifespan as an unresolved ForwardRef that is never rebuilt after FastMCP becomes available.","Calling Settings.model_rebuild() at the lazy import boundary in build_server() before FastMCP construction resolves the forward-reference and eliminates the warning.","A fresh-process facade contract test confirms build_server() succeeds with warning-as-error and emits the expected server name without suppression or dependency changes."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787589052376762001,"uuid":"7fb11922-815b-4058-8198-b29bbad4aee3"}